 Description 
Pillwort has slender, cylindrical, rush-like fronds up to {{convert|8|cm|in|abbr=on}} tall that are shaped like croziers as they unfurl. 
It has a pea-shaped, 4-chambered sporocarp about {{convert|3|mm|in|1|abbr=on}} in diameter, each chamber formed from a modified leaf and containing several sori bearing both megasporangia and microsporangia. The species is thus heterosporous.{{Citation needed|date=May 2021}}
